{"schema": 1, "ok": true, "kind": "physics", "tool": "", "title": "Motion in a plane", "order": 0, "indep": "t", "dep": "", "input_latex": "m\\,v_x' = -\\frac{G M m\\,x}{r^3},\\qquad m\\,v_y' = -\\frac{G M m\\,y}{r^3}", "normal_latex": "m\\,v_x' = -\\frac{G M m\\,x}{r^3},\\qquad m\\,v_y' = -\\frac{G M m\\,y}{r^3}", "rhs_expr": null, "ic": null, "summary": "Initial velocity along x = 0 m/s; Initial velocity along y = 7673 m/s; Mass of the central body = 5.972\u00d710^24 kg; Escape speed from the starting point = 10851 m/s; \u2026", "other_types": [], "methods": [{"id": "solve", "name": "Step by step", "applicable": true, "reason": "Newton's second law in two dimensions: mass times acceleration equals the sum of the forces.", "steps": [{"title": "Set up the equations of motion", "text": "Newton's second law along x and y. The central body at the origin attracts the particle with a force falling off as the square of the distance \\(r\\).", "latex": ["m\\,v_x' = -\\frac{G M m\\,x}{r^3},\\qquad m\\,v_y' = -\\frac{G M m\\,y}{r^3}", "v_x(0) = v_0\\cos\\theta,\\qquad v_y(0) = v_0\\sin\\theta"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Solve the equations", "text": "Energy and angular momentum are conserved, which fixes the shape of the orbit (a conic section) and its period. The position at a given time has no elementary formula, so it is found by numerical integration (fourth-order Runge-Kutta).", "latex": ["\\varepsilon = \\tfrac12 v^2 - \\frac{GM}{r},\\qquad h = x v_y - y v_x"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "List the known values", "text": "Everything is converted to SI units before it goes into the equations.", "latex": [], "substeps": [], "table": {"headers": ["\\text{quantity}", "\\text{symbol}", "\\text{given}", "\\text{SI}"], "rows": [["\\text{Gravitational parameter of the central body}", "GM", "398600\\ \\mathrm{km^3/s^2}", "3.986 \\times 10^{14}\\ \\mathrm{m^3/s^2}"], ["\\text{Initial x position}", "x_0", "6771\\ \\mathrm{km}", "6.771 \\times 10^{6}\\ \\mathrm{m}"], ["\\text{Initial y position}", "y_0", "0\\ \\mathrm{km}", "0\\ \\mathrm{m}"], ["\\text{Initial speed}", "v_0", "7.673\\ \\mathrm{km/s}", "7673\\ \\mathrm{m/s}"], ["\\text{Initial direction above the x axis}", "\\theta", "90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ}", "1.571\\ \\mathrm{rad}"]]}}, {"title": "Find the initial velocity along x", "text": "The x component of the initial velocity. With \\(v_0 = 7.673\\ \\mathrm{km/s}\\), \\(\\theta = 90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ}\\).", "latex": ["v_{x0} = v_0\\cos\\theta", "v_{x0} = 0\\ \\mathrm{m/s}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the initial velocity along y", "text": "The y component of the initial velocity. With \\(v_0 = 7.673\\ \\mathrm{km/s}\\), \\(\\theta = 90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ}\\).", "latex": ["v_{y0} = v_0\\sin\\theta", "v_{y0} = 7673\\ \\mathrm{m/s}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the mass of the central body", "text": "The gravitational parameter is Newton's constant times the central mass. With \\(GM = 398600\\ \\mathrm{km^3/s^2}\\).", "latex": ["M = \\frac{GM}{G}", "M = 5.972 \\times 10^{24}\\ \\mathrm{kg}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the escape speed from the starting point", "text": "Escape speed: kinetic energy just equal to the depth of the potential well. With \\(x_0 = 6771\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(y_0 = 0\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(GM = 398600\\ \\mathrm{km^3/s^2}\\).", "latex": ["v_{esc} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2GM}{r_0}},\\quad r_0 = \\sqrt{x_0^2 + y_0^2}", "v_{esc} = 10851\\ \\mathrm{m/s}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the energy per unit mass", "text": "Energy per unit mass is conserved along the orbit. With \\(x_0 = 6771\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(y_0 = 0\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(v_0 = 7.673\\ \\mathrm{km/s}\\), \\(GM = 398600\\ \\mathrm{km^3/s^2}\\).", "latex": ["\\varepsilon = \\tfrac12 v_0^2 - \\frac{GM}{r_0}", "\\varepsilon = -2.943 \\times 10^{7}\\ \\mathrm{J/kg}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the angular momentum per unit mass", "text": "Angular momentum per unit mass is conserved along the orbit. With \\(x_0 = 6771\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(y_0 = 0\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(v_0 = 7.673\\ \\mathrm{km/s}\\), \\(\\theta = 90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ}\\).", "latex": ["h = |x_0 v_{y0} - y_0 v_{x0}|", "h = 5.195 \\times 10^{10}\\ \\mathrm{m^2/s}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the eccentricity", "text": "The shape of the orbit from its energy and angular momentum. With \\(x_0 = 6771\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(y_0 = 0\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(v_0 = 7.673\\ \\mathrm{km/s}\\), \\(\\theta = 90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ}\\), \\(GM = 398600\\ \\mathrm{km^3/s^2}\\).", "latex": ["e = \\sqrt{1 + \\frac{2\\varepsilon h^2}{(GM)^2}}", "e = 0.0001057"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the closest distance (periapsis)", "text": "The closest approach. With \\(x_0 = 6771\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(y_0 = 0\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(v_0 = 7.673\\ \\mathrm{km/s}\\), \\(\\theta = 90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ}\\), \\(GM = 398600\\ \\mathrm{km^3/s^2}\\).", "latex": ["r_p = \\frac{h^2/GM}{1 + e}", "r_p = 6771\\ \\mathrm{km}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the farthest distance (apoapsis)", "text": "The farthest point (bound orbits only). With \\(x_0 = 6771\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(y_0 = 0\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(v_0 = 7.673\\ \\mathrm{km/s}\\), \\(\\theta = 90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ}\\), \\(GM = 398600\\ \\mathrm{km^3/s^2}\\).", "latex": ["r_a = \\frac{h^2/GM}{1 - e}", "r_a = 6772\\ \\mathrm{km}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Find the orbital period", "text": "Kepler's third law (bound orbits only). With \\(x_0 = 6771\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(y_0 = 0\\ \\mathrm{km}\\), \\(v_0 = 7.673\\ \\mathrm{km/s}\\), \\(\\theta = 90\\ \\mathrm{^\\circ}\\), \\(GM = 398600\\ \\mathrm{km^3/s^2}\\).", "latex": ["T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{a^3}{GM}},\\quad a = -\\frac{GM}{2\\varepsilon}", "T = 92.43\\ \\mathrm{min}"], "substeps": []}, {"title": "Summary", "text": "", "latex": [], "substeps": [], "table": {"headers": ["\\text{quantity}", "\\text{symbol}", "\\text{value}", ""], "rows": [["\\text{Mass}", "m", "\\text{--}", "\\text{not determined}"], ["\\text{Gravitational parameter of the c